<div id="apple-page" v-cloak>
  <div purpose="page-container">
    <div purpose="page-content">

      <div purpose="page-hero">
        <div purpose="hero-text">
          <h1>AI-native Apple device management</h1>
          <p>Patch apps, answer questions in seconds, and manage every Mac, iPhone, and iPad. Say what you need done, approve the change, and Fleet handles the rest.</p>
          <div purpose="button-row">
            <a purpose="cta-button" href="/contact?talkToUs">Get a demo</a>
            <animated-arrow-button href="/try">Try it yourself</animated-arrow-button>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div purpose="hero-image">
          <img alt="A Slack chat with Fleet. An admin asks which Macs in Engineering have an MCP server with shell access, and whether any of them are behind on macOS. Fleet reports that 14 of 1,120 Engineering Macs have one and 5 of those are still on macOS 15.7, then offers to propose a fix. The admin says yes, and Fleet proposes a policy and a macOS update deadline for their review." src="/images/hero-slack-demo-1080x643@2x.png">
        </div>
      </div>

      <div purpose="page-section">
        <div purpose="section-heading" class="left-aligned">
          <h2>Get AI working for you</h2>
          <p>Every setting in Fleet is a file and every feature has an API, so you can use AI to propose changes, with a human review between it and production.</p>
        </div>
        <div purpose="two-column-features">
          <div purpose="feature">
            <h5>Use AI to configure Apple devices</h5>
            <p>Generate configuration profiles and DDM declarations with prompts like <em>“Block iCloud Drive on company Macs”</em>. Use Claude, Cursor, or any AI harness.</p>
          </div>
          <div purpose="feature">
            <h5>Chat with your Macs</h5>
            <p>See what’s patched and what’s compliant without waiting hours. Investigate CVEs and supply chain issues in seconds.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div purpose="quote-and-logos">
        <div purpose="section-quote">
          <div purpose="quote-author-image">
            <img alt="Adam Anklewicz" src="/images/adam-anklewicz-120x120@2x.png">
          </div>
          <div purpose="quote-content">
            <p purpose="quote-text">“Before Fleet, a misconfiguration could hit every Mac in the company and be very hard to roll back safely. Now every change is reviewed before it ships, and if something’s wrong, we can revert it.”</p>
            <div purpose="name-and-title">
              <p purpose="author-name">Adam Anklewicz</p>
              <p purpose="author-title">Manager, IT Systems Engineering, Thumbtack</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div purpose="logo-grid">
          <div purpose="logo"><img height="22" alt="NVIDIA logo" src="/images/logos/logo-nvidia-color-161x32@2x.png"></div>
          <div purpose="logo"><img height="32" alt="Stripe logo" src="/images/stripe-logo-96x40@2x.png"></div>
          <div purpose="logo"><img height="24" alt="Reddit logo" src="/images/logo-reddit-96x28@2x.png"></div>
          <div purpose="logo"><img height="18" alt="Pinterest logo" src="/images/logo-pinterest-108x20@2x.png"></div>
          <div purpose="logo"><img height="40" alt="Epic Games logo" src="/images/logos/logo-epic-games-40x46@2x.png"></div>
          <div purpose="logo"><img height="24" alt="Mollie logo" src="/images/mollie-logo-136x40@2x.png"></div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div purpose="page-section">
        <div purpose="section-heading">
          <h2>Built for Apple</h2>
          <p>Apple depth, without an Apple-only tool. Fleet speaks Apple’s MDM and declarative device management protocols and reads live data from every Mac.</p>
        </div>
        <div purpose="pills">
          <span purpose="pill">macOS</span>
          <span purpose="pill">iOS and iPadOS</span>
          <span purpose="pill">Apple silicon and Intel</span>
          <span purpose="pill">Apple Business</span>
          <span purpose="pill">Automated Device Enrollment</span>
          <span purpose="pill">Declarative Device Management</span>
          <span purpose="pill">Platform SSO</span>
          <span purpose="pill">FileVault</span>
          <span purpose="pill">App Store apps</span>
          <span purpose="pill">Lost Mode</span>
          <span purpose="pill">Remote lock and wipe</span>
          <span purpose="pill">tvOS (coming soon)</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div purpose="feature-pair">
        <div purpose="feature-with-image">
          <div purpose="feature-image">
            <img alt="A list of AI tools Fleet found on Macs, including Claude Code, Cursor, GitHub Copilot, ChatGPT, and Ollama, with each tool's type." src="/images/feature-image-ai-tools-macos-504x378@2x.png">
          </div>
          <div purpose="feature-text">
            <div purpose="feature-heading">
              <h2>Your Macs are already <br purpose="desktop-break">running AI agents</h2>
              <p>Coding agents, MCP servers, and local models land on Macs long before anyone files a request. Fleet finds them across every user account, flags the risky ones, and turns any finding into a policy you can alert on.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div purpose="feature-with-image" class="reverse">
          <div purpose="feature-image">
            <img alt="Live results from Fleet's Get local administrator accounts on macOS report, listing each Mac, its admin account, and when it was last fetched." src="/images/feature-image-local-admins-macos-504x378@2x.png">
          </div>
          <div purpose="feature-text">
            <div purpose="feature-heading">
              <h2>Stop waiting for <br purpose="desktop-break">Jamf inventory updates</h2>
              <p>Fleet keeps a live connection to every Mac, so you see what’s actually on a device right now, not what it reported at the last inventory update. Ask a new question without writing an extension attribute first.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div purpose="feature-with-image">
          <div purpose="feature-image">
            <img alt="CIS benchmark policies for macOS in Fleet, with passing and failing host counts for each." src="/images/feature-image-cis-policies-macos-504x378@2x.png">
          </div>
          <div purpose="feature-text">
            <div purpose="feature-heading">
              <h2>Prove every Mac <br purpose="desktop-break">is compliant</h2>
              <p>Fleet ships CIS benchmarks for macOS and shows live pass/fail results for every Mac. Macs that fail can be blocked from company apps through your IdP, and employees see how to fix the problem themselves in Fleet Desktop.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div purpose="quote-section">
        <p purpose="quote-text">“Someone’s up and running on their laptop in about 20 minutes, with the right software and the right identity groups. In Jamf that was a day or two of lost productivity.”</p>
        <div purpose="quote-author-info">
          <div purpose="quote-author-image">
            <img alt="Robbie Trencheny" src="/images/robbie-trencheny-120x120@2x.png">
          </div>
          <div purpose="name-and-title">
            <p purpose="author-name">Robbie Trencheny</p>
            <p purpose="author-title">Head of Infrastructure and IT</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div purpose="feature-with-image" class="reverse">
        <div purpose="feature-image">
          <img alt="A new Mac's setup screen in Fleet, installing apps and running a script before the employee reaches the desktop." src="/images/feature-image-setup-experience-macos-504x378@2x.png">
        </div>
        <div purpose="feature-text">
          <div purpose="feature-heading">
            <h2>Every new Mac ready <br purpose="desktop-break">before the first login</h2>
            <p>Assigned Macs, iPhones, and iPads show up in Fleet before they’re unboxed. Employees sign in with their IdP account, and Fleet names the Mac account to match, installs what they need, and puts each device in the right fleet. After that, the Mac password stays in sync with the IdP.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div purpose="feature-with-image">
        <div purpose="feature-image">
          <img alt="Fleet's OS updates page, showing current macOS versions with host counts and a target minimum version and deadline." src="/images/feature-image-os-updates-macos-504x378@2x.png">
        </div>
        <div purpose="feature-text">
          <div purpose="feature-heading">
            <h2>Get every Mac on the <br purpose="desktop-break">latest macOS</h2>
            <p>Users can click “Later” until the deadline, and then the update installs. Declarative device management enforces macOS, iOS, and iPadOS versions by the date you set, with no extra tools to maintain.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div purpose="feature-with-image" class="reverse">
        <div purpose="feature-image">
          <img alt="" src="/images/feature-image-patch-without-breaking-504x378@2x.png">
        </div>
        <div purpose="feature-text">
          <div purpose="feature-heading">
            <h2>Patch without breaking <br purpose="desktop-break">anyone’s day</h2>
            <p>Fleet maintains 980+ Mac apps and keeps them patched automatically. Queue an update for when the app is closed, patch right away when a vulnerability can’t wait, or pin a version until change control signs off.</p>
          </div>
          <animated-arrow-button href="/software-catalog">Software catalog</animated-arrow-button>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div purpose="migration-banner">
        <div purpose="banner-image">
          <img alt="" src="/images/migration-banner-366x225@2x.png">
        </div>
        <div purpose="banner-text">
          <h3>Moving off Jamf, Kandji, or Workspace ONE?</h3>
          <p>Apple’s built-in migration in macOS 26, iOS 26, and iPadOS 26 brings devices over to Fleet without a wipe. Migrate in batches, so nothing goes unmanaged in between.</p>
          <a purpose="cta-button" href="/contact?talkToUs">Get a demo</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div purpose="feature-with-image" class="reverse">
        <div purpose="photo-collage">
          <img purpose="photo-celebration" alt="A Fleet workshop attendee" src="/images/fast-track-certification-celebration-600x450@2x.jpg">
          <img purpose="photo-classroom" alt="Fleet workshop attendees" src="/images/fast-track-certification-classroom-600x450@2x.jpg">
          <img purpose="photo-training" alt="Fleet workshop attendees" src="/images/fast-track-certification-training-400x533@2x.jpg">
        </div>
        <div purpose="feature-text">
          <h2>Get certified</h2>
          <div purpose="checklist">
            <p>Earn certification you can add to your LinkedIn profile to demonstrate your proficiency with AI-native Apple device management.</p>
            <p>Practice new AI-native techniques for managing Macs, iPhones, and iPads, developed by the IT teams at leading tech companies.</p>
          </div>
          <animated-arrow-button href="/workshops">Free workshops</animated-arrow-button>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div purpose="faq-section">
        <h2>FAQ</h2>
        <div purpose="accordion">
          <div purpose="accordion-item">
            <p purpose="accordion-header" id="accordion__header-faq-1" class="accordion" data-toggle="collapse" data-target="#accordion__body-faq-1" aria-controls="accordion__body-faq-1">
              Does Fleet replace Jamf?
              <span class="fa fa-angle-down"></span>
            </p>
            <div purpose="accordion-answer" id="accordion__body-faq-1" class="collapse" aria-labelledby="accordion__header-faq-1">
              <p>Yes. Fleet manages Macs, iPhones, and iPads with Apple’s MDM and declarative device management, and manages Windows, Linux, and Android from the same place. Many teams replace Jamf and the second tool they use for everything else.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div purpose="accordion-item">
            <p purpose="accordion-header" id="accordion__header-faq-2" class="accordion" data-toggle="collapse" data-target="#accordion__body-faq-2" aria-controls="accordion__body-faq-2">
              Can I run Fleet alongside my current MDM?
              <span class="fa fa-angle-down"></span>
            </p>
            <div purpose="accordion-answer" id="accordion__body-faq-2" class="collapse" aria-labelledby="accordion__header-faq-2">
              <p>Yes. Fleet’s agent runs alongside Jamf or another MDM, so you get live reports, policies, and scripts without changing anything else. Apple allows only one MDM at a time, so your current MDM can stay in place while you evaluate. When you’re ready, Apple’s built-in migration moves devices over without a wipe.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div purpose="accordion-item">
            <p purpose="accordion-header" id="accordion__header-faq-3" class="accordion" data-toggle="collapse" data-target="#accordion__body-faq-3" aria-controls="accordion__body-faq-3">
              Which Apple platforms does Fleet support?
              <span class="fa fa-angle-down"></span>
            </p>
            <div purpose="accordion-answer" id="accordion__body-faq-3" class="collapse" aria-labelledby="accordion__header-faq-3">
              <p>Macs get MDM plus Fleet’s agent. iPhones and iPads are managed with MDM only.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div purpose="accordion-item">
            <p purpose="accordion-header" id="accordion__header-faq-4" class="accordion" data-toggle="collapse" data-target="#accordion__body-faq-4" aria-controls="accordion__body-faq-4">
              Can employees enroll personal iPhones and iPads?
              <span class="fa fa-angle-down"></span>
            </p>
            <div purpose="accordion-answer" id="accordion__body-faq-4" class="collapse" aria-labelledby="accordion__header-faq-4">
              <p>Yes. User Enrollment with a Managed Apple Account keeps work data separate.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div purpose="accordion-item">
            <p purpose="accordion-header" id="accordion__header-faq-8" class="accordion" data-toggle="collapse" data-target="#accordion__body-faq-8" aria-controls="accordion__body-faq-8">
              How do I deploy apps to iPhones and iPads?
              <span class="fa fa-angle-down"></span>
            </p>
            <div purpose="accordion-answer" id="accordion__body-faq-8" class="collapse" aria-labelledby="accordion__header-faq-8">
              <p>See the guides to <a href="/guides/install-app-store-apps">installing App Store apps</a> and <a href="/guides/deploy-software-packages">deploying in-house apps</a>.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div purpose="accordion-item">
            <p purpose="accordion-header" id="accordion__header-faq-5" class="accordion" data-toggle="collapse" data-target="#accordion__body-faq-5" aria-controls="accordion__body-faq-5">
              What about Macs that aren’t in Apple Business?
              <span class="fa fa-angle-down"></span>
            </p>
            <div purpose="accordion-answer" id="accordion__body-faq-5" class="collapse" aria-labelledby="accordion__header-faq-5">
              <p>Employees turn on MDM themselves from Fleet Desktop.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div purpose="accordion-item">
            <p purpose="accordion-header" id="accordion__header-faq-6" class="accordion" data-toggle="collapse" data-target="#accordion__body-faq-6" aria-controls="accordion__body-faq-6">
              Can Fleet work with Munki, Puppet, or Chef?
              <span class="fa fa-angle-down"></span>
            </p>
            <div purpose="accordion-answer" id="accordion__body-faq-6" class="collapse" aria-labelledby="accordion__header-faq-6">
              <p>Yes, via a bootstrap package.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div purpose="accordion-item">
            <p purpose="accordion-header" id="accordion__header-faq-7" class="accordion" data-toggle="collapse" data-target="#accordion__body-faq-7" aria-controls="accordion__body-faq-7">
              Can I manage multiple Apple Business accounts?
              <span class="fa fa-angle-down"></span>
            </p>
            <div purpose="accordion-answer" id="accordion__body-faq-7" class="collapse" aria-labelledby="accordion__header-faq-7">
              <p>Yes, for MSPs and subsidiaries.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <p purpose="faq-note">Couldn’t find an answer? <a href="/contact?sendMessage">Message us</a></p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div purpose="bottom-cta">
        <h1>AI-native Apple device management</h1>
        <div purpose="button-row">
          <a purpose="cta-button" href="/contact?talkToUs">Get a demo</a>
          <animated-arrow-button href="/try">Try it yourself</animated-arrow-button>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
